<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Rana Sanga</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1482–1528</span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a> · Also known as Sangram Singh I</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Rana Sanga was the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sisodia">Sisodia</a> ruler of Mewar from 1508 to 1528 and the leading <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rajputs">Rajput</a> king of his time. He defeated the sultans of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/malwa">Malwa</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gujarat">Gujarat</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/delhi">Delhi</a> and built a wide coalition of Rajput clans. In 1527 he led this coalition against the Mughal founder <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/babur">Babur</a> at the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-khanwa">Battle of Khanwa</a>, where he was defeated; he died the next year.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/rana-sanga.jpg" alt="Rana Sanga" width="320" height="511" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Aristocratic 536 · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Photo_of_Rana_Sanga_from_Udaipur_Museum_(From_my_Camera).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
